# Integrity Constraints
- set of rules that are applied on the table or relationships
- ensure that the overall validity, integrity and consistency
- mechanism to prevent invalid data entries in the database
1. Entity Integrity Constraints
- fundamental concept in relational database 
- ensures each row(tuple) in a table is uniquely identifiable.
  i. PRIMARY KEY Constraints
  ii. UNIQUE KEY Concstraints
2. Domain Integrity Constraint
- ensure only the valid domain/range of values can be stored in a column
- prevent unnecessary manipulation of data at the column level.
  i. NOT NULL
  ii. CHECK
  iii. DEFAULT
3. Referential Integrity Constraints
- ensures relationships between tables remain valid
- prevent invalid references and maintaining data consistency across the database.
 i. CASCADE UPDATE
    - if there is some change in primary key of a certain table then changes will be seem
     automatically in the foreign key on another table regerencing to that primary key.
     - Syntax: ON UPDATE CASCADE (after the reference)
 ii. CASCADE DELETE
    - if primary key row/record of certain table is deleted then it will automatically delete
     all the records referencing to that primary key.
     - Syntax: ON DELETE CASCADE (after the reference) 
